# Independent Metrics measured-evidence audit

The frozen 2,217-artifact review was authenticated before and after arithmetic recomputation. The 1,006 current study copies also match the unchanged source study. All 117 readiness artifacts, seven fixed workload specifications and 14 input/expected files remain exact. Six original files match their official release/dependency archive members; both archive SHA-256 and registry SHA-512 identities and the local Node executable identity were rechecked without executing original code.

Independent arithmetic from retained raw records matches all seven timing rows, seven memory rows and 147 signed per-child rows. Counts are 147 timing children, 147 memory children, 1,323 timing fresh/cache packet comparisons, 1,311,282 memory comparisons and 1,987 PID observer samples. The 887 new measurement artifacts include 294 timing child logs and 588 memory child/observer logs. All children completed; no failed/partial/killed/limit-hit child is hidden. The 27 negative signed child metrics, 845 negative paired differences and 686 unavailable zero-control percentages remain distinct and unclipped. Unavailable derived percentages are not censored child results.

For all percentiles, candidate median 2.7655 ms/call versus baseline 2.004033333 ms gives +37.99670664% as a ratio of medians. The median paired percentage is separately +6.09104972%; five of seven repetitions are slower and observed ranges overlap. Single-p95 lifetime RSS median is 93.7109375 MiB versus baseline 90.34765625 MiB. None of these seven-repetition descriptive observations establishes a cause, confidence interval, full nonregression, allocation superiority or candidate acceptance.

Timing children load all three implementations for common correctness prevalidation; their memory diagnostics are not isolated. Memory children select one implementation. Release/retention deltas include GC and common post-retention packet/cache serialization. The 100 ms numeric-PID observer and checkpoints can miss peaks; complete-child lifetime RSS is different. No process-start identity, OS resource sandbox, cumulative allocation guarantee or outer memory-controller watchdog is claimed.

No reducer, workload generator, stage module, measurement child, test, browser or profiler was executed by this audit. The audit only hashes bytes, parses retained observations/archive members and performs arithmetic. The initial read-only lookup assumed the wrong receipt filename; it is recorded as a lookup error, not a candidate failure. Production, frozen stage, previous evidence and thresholds remain unchanged. Candidate acceptance and full-product/superiority gates remain false.

`audit-validation.json` binds the checked stage and records the finite conclusions. `recomputed-statistics.json` preserves every recomputed value. `preservation-manifest.json` binds all four audit files; `freeze.json` binds the receipt and manifest.
